## 🚫 Unicode Emoji Policy (CODE FILES ONLY)

**This policy applies to CODE and SCRIPTS only** (`.ps1`, `.py`, `.sh`, `.bat`)

**Markdown files (`.md`) can use any emoji** - browsers and editors render them fine.

**In CODE, only these emojis are safe:**

| Category | Allowed |
|----------|---------|
| Status | ✅ ❌ ⚠️ ✓ ✗ |
| Documents | 📚 📁 📋 📦 📊 📄 |
| Actions | 🎯 🚀 💡 🔗 🔧 ⚙️ |
| Development | 🛠️ 🧪 🏗️ 💻 |
| Celebration | ✨ 🎉 🎵 |
| Arrows | ▶ ◀ ▲ ▼ → ← ↑ ↓ |
| Other | 💪 🤖 🌐 💬 🔒 🔑 |

**Why?** Terminal fonts and CI logs may render exotic emojis as boxes.
**In code:** When in doubt, use ASCII or the allowed list above.

